Overlay patch 0023: thread-safe CVar map (LUS ConsoleVariable) — SYNC WAVE 2
item 1 (reference 0030, commit 0bafc69). CRITICAL: a latent SEGV every port
ships. SoH crashed twice in one session (death, pause) with SIGSEGV at
CVarGetInteger on the audio thread: the synth reads CVars every audio update
while the main thread writes them (menu interaction, death sequence, pause
open). ConsoleVariable::mVariables is a bare std::unordered_map — a
concurrent insert rehashes while the audio thread is inside find() ->
freed-bucket deref -> SEGV. Starship has the SAME architecture: its audio
worker (GameEngine::HandleAudioThread, a game-side std::thread) runs the
recompiled SF64 synth, which reads CVars per update, while the main thread
writes them. Fix: a recursive_mutex over every mVariables access. All reads
funnel through Get(); writes are the five Set*, ClearVariable, CopyVariable,
Save (iteration), Load (clear). recursive_mutex because
Register*/ClearVariable/Load re-enter via Get()/Set*(). LoadFromPath and
ClearBlock touch mVariables only through Set*/Load (already locked) or not at
all. Uncontended lock cost is tens of ns against hundreds of calls/frame.
Fork note: Starship's LUS (Kenix3) ConsoleVariable is at src/config/ (not
src/ship/config/) and its mVariables has no TransparentStringHash — asserted
below.

